      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Cost Factors in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size and Complexity: A standard two-story asphalt shingle home (1,500\u20132,500 sq ft) takes about 60 to 90 minutes to check. Large or highly complex layouts with multiple dormers or steep slopes take longer and cost more ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Specialized Materials: Standard asphalt shingles require no premium. Delicate or complex materials like clay tile, wood shake, or slate require specialized safety equipment and command a $25 to $75 premium."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Certifications: If you need a formal \"roof certification\" for a lender or a real estate transaction to guarantee the roof will last 2\u20135 years, expect an additional $75 to $200 surcharge on top of the inspection fee."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Urgency & Storms: Following major Wasatch Front wind or hail storms, high demand can spike prices. Emergency or immediate post-storm leak inspections often incur a $100 to $300 surcharge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "When is an inspection free?"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You should avoid paying a standalone inspection fee under two common scenarios:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contractor Bids: If you are actively looking to repair or replace your roof, most reputable local roofing companies offer free detailed inspections because they hope to earn your business for the actual physical work ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Claims: If your roof suffered obvious wind or hail damage, your insurance adjuster will perform the inspection for free as part of processing your storm claim."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down the best approach, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is your primary reason for the inspection? (e.g., buying/selling a home, storm damage, active leak, or routine check)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What type of roofing material do you have? (e.g., asphalt shingle, tile, metal, or flat)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Approximately how old is the current roof?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help guide you on whether you need a certified independent inspector or a free contractor estimate."
      }
